# A night club lit by saturated LEDs: magenta, cyan, deep blue and green light that cameras record far outside
# what a display can show. Ungraded, those colours clip into flat blobs and shift hue (blue turns purple, red turns
# orange). The grade first brings them back into gamut, then builds the look round them.
#   tame_leds     gamut compression first: the most saturated colours are pulled in toward the gamut boundary
#                 (only the outer few percent move), so the LEDs keep their texture and their hue
#   deep_blacks   a club is dark: crush the deep shadows a little, keep the mids
#   neon_palette  pull the palette to the club's two colours: greens toward cyan, reds and oranges toward magenta
#   led_glow      a big, soft glow like light in smoke, only from the lights themselves: keyed in RGB (red OR green
#                 OR blue channel high) OR by high saturation (a qualifier over every hue)
#   richer_mids   more colour in the mids, less in the deep shadows
#   skin_back     skin keyed and calmed back, so faces under the LEDs keep their own colour
#   film_grain    fine grain, a little colour: club footage is shot at a high ISO
# Use it for club, concert and music-video footage; on footage without strong coloured light it does little.
cierra 0.1
name "neon club"
about "Gamut compression first, deep blacks, cyan-magenta palette, bloom on the LEDs, grain."
input aces2065_1
output aces2(display: rec1886)

node tame_leds = gamut_compress(threshold: [0.75, 0.75, 0.8], power: 1.3)
  label "LEDs back into gamut, hue kept"
node deep_blacks = curve(points: [[0.0729, 0.0729], [0.18, 0.15], [0.3, 0.28], [0.4136, 0.42], [0.8, 0.82]])
node neon_palette = hue_vs_hue(points: [[206, 35, 45], [150, -40, 30], [123, -30, 25]])
  label "greens to cyan, oranges and reds to magenta"
node led_glow = glow(threshold: 0.5, radius_px: 60, strength: 0.4)
  label "haze glow on the lights"
  mask rgb_key(red: 0.62..1.5, soft: 0.08) or rgb_key(green: 0.62..1.5, soft: 0.08) or rgb_key(blue: 0.62..1.5, soft: 0.08) or qualifier(hue: 0..360, sat: 0.12..1, soft: 0.1)
node richer_mids = lum_vs_sat(points: [[0.15, 0.9], [0.4, 1.15], [0.7, 1.05]])
node skin_back = saturation(amount: 0.85)
  label "skin back to its own colour"
  mask skin(width: 30)
node film_grain = grain(amount: 0.18, size_px: 1.5, chroma: 0.4, seed: 2077)

graph tame_leds -> deep_blacks -> neon_palette -> led_glow -> richer_mids -> skin_back -> film_grain
